# EXPECT: assigns module name 'z' that it also interrogates
# (round 197, #218) A function that assigns a MODULE name it also interrogates:
# on the VM the interrogated name binds function-local (#99 escape pre-scan),
# so `print of z` after the call is the OLD module value; the AOT wrote the
# module binding (0.25). Refused by name until the per-call env (Part 2b).
z is 1.0
define u() as:
    z is 0.25
    return prev of z
print of (u of [])
print of z
